 "interpretationRules": {
  "encodedRules": [],
  "sourceGuidance": [
   {
    "title": "IRIS Scoring & Interpretation",
    "text": "IRIS results are presented as two subscale scores:\n\nAlcohol and other drug risk : (items 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7) The Alcohol and Other Drug risk subscale ranges from 7-28, with higher scores reflecting a greater likelihood of problematic alcohol and drug use as well as dependence. Scores of 10 or more represent clinically significant risk.\nMental health and emotional well-being risk : (items 8, 9, 10, 11, 12, 13) The Mental Health risk subscale ranges from 6-18, with higher scores indicating increased risks of a psychological condition or functional impairment (Schlesinger et al., 2007; Marel et al., n.d.). Scores of 11 or more represent clinically significant risk, with the client being likely to have a ICD-10 depression or anxiety disorder (with a sensitivity of 83% and a specificity of 84% in relation to a psychiatric interview using ICD-10 diagnostic criteria for depression and anxiety disorders).\nIf administered more than once a line graph will be produced for each subscale score.\n\n",
    "source_url": null
   }
  ],
  "reportScoringGuidance": [
   {
    "documentSha256": "7b274daa31e178c0af6aee7378e0ac3bcec3d251ebda2e83f4b58affe4fcee4a",
    "pageNumber": 2,
    "text": "For comprehensive information on the IRIS, \nsee here\n.\nIRIS results are presented as two subscale scores: Alcohol and other drug risk: (items 1, 2, 3, 4,\n5, 6, 7) The Alcohol and Other Drug risk subscale ranges from 7-28, with higher scores\nreflecting a greater likelihood of problematic alcohol and drug use as well as dependence.\nScores of 10 or more represent clinically significant risk. Mental health and emotional well-being\nrisk: (items 8, 9, 10, 11, 12, 13) The Mental Health risk subscale ranges from 6-18, with higher\nscores indicating increased risks of a psychological condition or functional impairment\n(Schlesinger et al., 2007; Marel et al., n.d.). Scores of 11 or more represent clinically significant\nrisk, with the client being likely to have a ICD-10 depression or anxiety disorder (with a\nsensitivity of 83% and a specificity of 84% in relation to a psychiatric interview using ICD-10\ndiagnostic criteria for depression and anxiety disorders).",
    "usage": "source_guidance_for_review_not_executable_scoring",
    "runtimeEnabled": false
   }
  ],
  "sourceRequirements": [
   "If administered more than once a line graph will be produced for each subscale score."
  ],
